<article class="reading">
  <h1>Values</h1>

  <p>I design products that make complex systems feel simple. I've led product design across industries, from dev tools to healthcare. I move fast without cutting corners.</p>

  <p>I work across the full product lifecycle: from shaping problems with PMs and researchers to sweating engineering details that bring the design to life.</p>

  <section class="values-section" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="approach-heading"><span class="section-heading__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><span class="section-heading__text">How I Approach Product Design (Without the Double Diamond)</span></h2>
    <p>My primary job as a designer is to enable others to see the future. To see what could be. To help the team make better decisions faster and ultimately make our customers feel like they're in control when using our designs.</p>

    <p>A few things I believe:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Design is decision-making.</strong> Tools and trends come and go. What stays: the ability to clarify tradeoffs, prioritize, and rally a team around what matters. AI is changing how we build, but the fundamentals of good design haven't changed.</li>
      <li><strong>Prototypes beat meetings.</strong> A good prototype shortens debate cycles and gets real feedback faster than a slide deck ever could.</li>
      <li><strong>Taste matters.</strong> I care about polish. Not for its own sake, but because details shape trust and usability.</li>
      <li><strong>Process is a tool, not a religion.</strong> I've run structured design sprints and loose async design reviews. The team and problem define the process, not the other way around.</li>
      <li><strong>The future belongs to generalists.</strong> Ai gives everyone the ability to do more. Code, sales, marketing, animation, operations, presenting, writing. Designers don't have to do it all, but producing artwork isn't enough on its own.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="values-section" aria-labelledby="teams-heading">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="teams-heading"><span class="section-heading__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><span class="section-heading__text">How I Work Across Teams</span></h2>
    <ul>
      <li>I work with PMs to shape product direction, clarify tradeoffs, and balance business goals with user needs.</li>
      <li>I partner with engineers early, providing context and detail so they can build confidently, and ensure what ships is what we actually designed.</li>
      <li>I bring stakeholders into the process early so we're aligned before the pixels even hit the screen.</li>
      <li>I involve the full team in ideation and reviews, sharing work early, even when "it's not ready yet!", to build trust and momentum.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p>Good design is clarity, not decoration. It's making things make sense, internally and externally. That's the work I care about.</p>
</article>
